' SiO2alpha NCSU       EVAL-MAY11 Holmes, Al-Qasir, Hehr, Hawari     '
' REF. 2 (2008)        DIST-                                         '
'----ENDF/B-VIII.beta  MATERIAL 47                                   '
'-----THERMAL NEUTRON SCATTERING DATA                                '
'------ENDF-6 FORMAT                                                 '
'                                                                    '
' Temperatures = 293.6 350 400 500 800 K                             '
'                                                                    '
' History                                                            '
' -------                                                            '
' This library was produced at North Carolina State University in    '
' May 2011.  The VASP and PHONON codes were used to produce the      '
' DOS for O-16 and natural Si in SiO2.  The alpha-quartz phase       '
' is treated for all temperatures in this library.  The beta-        '
' quartz phase is treated for 1000 K and 1100 K in a separate        '
' library to allow incorporation of phase-specific Bragg edge        '
' energy grids.  The LEAPR module was used to produce File 7         '
' MT = 2, 4 data for SiO2 as a mixed moderator.  Modifications to    '
' the LEAPR source code were made to calculate the                   '
' crystallographic structure factors for alpha-quartz for MT = 2     '
' data.  Modifications to the normal LEAPR card input were made      '
' to correct for issues with LEAPR that apply only to mixed          '
' moderators with non-1:1 stoichiometry.  Details of these           '
' modifications can be found in Ref. 1, Appendix A.  By              '
' convention, compounds have MAT numbers ranging from 1-99.  This    '
' range is subdivided by material category.  The current ENDF        '
' manual (BNL-90365-2009 Rev. 2) assigns MAT = 47 to O in SiO2       '
' under the Oxygen category (MAT = 45-50) since SiO2 clearly does    '
' not fall into any other existing category.  However, note that     '
' this library uses MAT = 47 for a whole-molecule treatment of       '
' alpha-quartz with Si as the primary scatterer.  Following          '
' convention for compounds, ZA = MAT + 100 = 147 is used.  When      '
' processing with THERMR, the PENDF file used should be for          '
' natural Si (or Si-28, if desired).  Also in THERMR and ACER,       '
' MT = 247/248 (which are unassigned and not previously used) may    '
' be selected for inelastic/elastic scattering reaction              '
' types for alpha-quartz until permanent ENDF reaction type          '
' numbers are assigned.  If an ACE library is to be produced,        '
' use NMIX = 3 on Card 9 in ACER.  See Ref. 1, Appendix A for        '
' explanation.                                                       '
'                                                                    '
' Theory                                                             '
' ------                                                             '
' Both the alpha and beta polymorphic phases of quartz (SiO2) can    '
' be viewed on a hexagonal lattice system and have unit cell         '
' stoichiometry of Si3O6 (nine atoms).  (Data in this library is     '
' associated with the three-atom SiO2 unit).  Alpha-quartz is of     '
' the trigonal crystal system with three-fold symmetry while         '
' beta-quartz is of the hexagonal crystal system with six-fold       '
' symmetry.  The alpha-quartz to beta-quartz phase transformation    '
' occurs completely and almost instantaneously at 846 K and is       '
' identically reversible.  The transition occurs through a slight    '
' realignment of SiO4 tetrahedra which increases the Si-O-Si bond    '
' angle from 144 deg. to 153 deg. and reduces density from about     '
' 2.65 g/cm^3 to 2.53 g/cm^3.                                        '
'                                                                    '
' References                                                         '
' ----------                                                         '
' 1. J. C. Holmes, Development of ENDF Thermal Neutron Scattering    '
'    Libraries for Silicon Dioxide and MCNP Criticality Testing      '
'    with an ICSBEP Benchmark, North Carolina State University       '
'    (2011).                                                         '
' 2. B. D. Hehr, A. I. Hawari, "Calculation of the Thermal           '
'    Neutron Scattering Cross Section of Alpha Quartz,"              '
'    Proceedings of PHYSOR 2008:  Nuclear Power -- A Sustainable     '
'    Resource (2008).                                                '
' 3. A. I. Hawari, I. I. Al-Qasir, V. H. Gillette, B. W. Wehring     '
'    and T. Zhou, "Ab Initio Generation of Thermal Neutron           '
'    Scattering Cross Sections," Proceedings of PHYSOR 2004:  The    '
'    Physics of Fuel Cycles and Advanced Nuclear Systems --          '
'    Global Developments (2004).                                     '
/
